# data-models-relationships

## Core Data Models

### Treatment Facilities
- Multi-dimensional classification system for facility types:
  - Treatment modalities (residential, outpatient, detox)
  - Population served (men, women, couples, youth)
  - Service types (MAT, counseling, therapy)
- Verification workflow states with required documentation
- Network affiliations and insurance acceptance tracking
- County-specific service area mapping

### Legal Cases
- Case type initialization for:
  - Custody reunification 
  - Record expungement
- Milestone tracking with verification requirements
- Required document categories per case type
- Custom workflow states for document processing

### Community Resources
- Pin categorization system:
  - Safe zones
  - Food/water access
  - Charging/wifi
  - Bathrooms
  - Warning alerts
- Verification states for community-submitted locations
- Real-time reliability scoring
- Geographic clustering rules

## Key Relationships

### Treatment Verification Flow
- Provider -> Document -> Verification State
- Provider -> Service Area -> County
- Provider -> Insurance -> Network Status

### Legal Case Processing
- Case -> Required Documents
- Case -> Milestones
- Case -> Calendar Events
- Case -> Resource Referrals

### Resource Management
- Pin -> Verification Status
- Pin -> Community Comments
- Pin -> Safety Rating
- Pin -> Service Category

